      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2025-june/q3",
      "question": "<p>Given</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;5\\\\0&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>prove by mathematical induction that, for <span data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^n=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;5(2^n-1)\\\\0&amp;2^n\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol><p>Given</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf B=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li><p>describe fully the single geometrical transformation <span data-math=\"P\"></span> represented by the matrix <span data-math=\"\\mathbf B\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The transformation <span data-math=\"Q\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span data-math=\"\\mathbf A^n\"></span></p><p>The transformation <span data-math=\"P\"></span> followed by the transformation <span data-math=\"Q\"></span> is the transformation <span data-math=\"R\"></span>, which is represented by the matrix <span data-math=\"\\mathbf C\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li><p>Determine <span data-math=\"\\mathbf C\"></span> in terms of <span data-math=\"n\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>Given that, for a particular value of <span data-math=\"n\"></span>, the transformation <span data-math=\"R\"></span> maps the point with coordinates <span data-math=\"(27,1)\"></span> to the point with coordinates <span data-math=\"(a,a)\"></span>, where <span data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"4\"><li><p>determine the matrix that represents the transformation <span data-math=\"Q\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
