      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2025-june/q6",
      "question": "<p>The quartic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x^4+Ax^3-Ax^2-5x+6=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span data-math=\"A\"></span> is a real constant, has roots <span data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, <span data-math=\"\\beta\"></span>, <span data-math=\"\\gamma\"></span> and <span data-math=\"\\delta\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Determine the value of</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac3\\alpha+\\frac3\\beta+\\frac3\\gamma+\\frac3\\delta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Given that <span data-math=\"\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2+\\delta^2=-\\dfrac34\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li><p>determine the possible values of <span data-math=\"A\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
