      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\"><img style=\"width:82mm;max-width:100%;height:auto\" src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-02-2025-june/q7-figure.png\" alt=\"Figure 1: polar curve C with a cusp at O and symmetric points A and B at the left and right extremes. The initial line extends horizontally right from O.\"></figure><p>The curve <span data-math=\"C\"></span> shown in Figure 1 has polar equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=a(1+\\sin\\theta)\\qquad-\\pi&lt;\\theta\\leqslant\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>The tangents to <span data-math=\"C\"></span> at the points <span data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span data-math=\"B\"></span> are perpendicular to the initial line.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Use calculus to determine the polar coordinates of <span data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span data-math=\"B\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol><p>The curve <span data-math=\"C\"></span> models the perimeter of the surface of a swimming pool.</p><p>Given that, according to the model, the distance across the pool from <span data-math=\"A\"></span> to <span data-math=\"B\"></span> is 10 m,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li><p>show that <span data-math=\"a=\\dfrac{20\\sqrt3}{9}\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li><p>Use algebraic integration to determine the surface area of the swimming pool, according to the model.</p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
